[1138, 1022], [1411, 1030], [1410, 1062], [1137, 1054]]}, {"text": "f) -2 × [(1 + (-3)] = (-2 × 1) + [(-2 × (-3)]", "conf": 0.861, "box": [[212, 1043], [851, 1060], [850, 1097], [211, 1080]]}, {"text": "How we can dividetwo", "conf": 0.859, "box": [[1135, 1061], [1469, 1070], [1468, 1103], [1134, 1094]]}, {"text": "g) [(-7) = 1)] × (-3) = [(-7) × (-3)] -[1 × (-3)]", "conf": 0.857, "box": [[211, 1099], [906, 1116], [906, 1155], [210, 1138]]}, {"text": "whole numbers?", "conf": 0.866, "box": [[1137, 1102], [1370, 1108], [1370, 1141], [1136, 1135]]}, {"text": "Write any two numbers and", "conf": 0.836, "box": [[1137, 1142], [1534, 1153], [1533, 1186], [1136, 1176]]}, {"text": "h) -4 × [(7 + (-8)] = (-4 × 7) + [(-4 × (-8)]", "conf": 0.881, "box": [[211, 1153], [868, 1173], [867, 1208], [210, 1189]]}, {"text": "divide them step by step.", "conf": 0.841, "box": [[1139, 1182], [1494, 1197], [1493, 1226], [1137, 1212]]}, {"text": "3.6 Divisionof Integers", "conf": 0.862, "box": [[571, 1233], [1110, 1256], [1108, 1302], [569, 1279]]}, {"text": "3.6.1RelationofMultiplicationand Division", "conf": 0.894, "box": [[118, 1289], [964, 1319], [962, 1359], [117, 1328]]}, {"text": "We have learned how to multiply and divide numbers in previous grades. These two", "conf": 0.947, "box": [[119, 1343], [1443, 1396], [1441, 1438], [118, 1385]]}, {"text": "operations are inverse of each other. We know that an", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[120, 1399], [956, 1429], [954, 1469], [119, 1439]]}, {"text": "inverse operation in Mathematics means an operation that", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[118, 1451], [1029, 1488], [1027, 1527], [117, 1490]]}, {"text": "reverses the effect of an earlier operation.", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[119, 1504], [759, 1531], [758, 1568], [118, 1541]]}, {"text": "For example, when 3 is multiplied to number 4, we get 12. Now if 12 is divided by 3, we get", "conf": 0.934, "box": [[117, 1549], [1566, 1618], [1564, 1667], [114, 1597]]}, {"text": "the original number 4. So the division reversed the process of multiplication and result is", "conf": 0.939, "box": [[118, 1605], [1520, 1670], [1518, 1714], [116, 1648]]}, {"text": "the original number 4.", "conf": 0.89, "box": [[119, 1663], [458, 1676], [456, 1713], [118, 1699]]}, {"text": "3.6.2Division of Integers", "conf": 0.909, "box": [[117, 1714], [591, 1736], [589, 1779], [115, 1757]]}, {"text": "When we divide two integers, we follow these rules.", "conf": 0.898, "box": [[119, 1773], [913, 1810], [911, 1850], [117, 1813]]}, {"text": "1. The quotient of two positive integers will be a positive integer.", "conf": 0.932, "box": [[118, 1820], [1126, 1874], [1124, 1922], [115, 1868]]}, {"text": "56", "conf": 0.665, "box": [[783, 1988], [834, 1988], [834, 2028], [783, 2028]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.817, "box": [[1155, 2017], [1455, 2036], [1453, 2069], [1153, 2050]]}]}